    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d567">

                <pb facs="0638" n="626" sameAs="frus:frus1943v05/pg626"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.24532/25</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Caffery</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 10866</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Rio de
                                Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-04-17">April 17, 1943</date>.<lb/>[Received April
                        23.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to recent reports concerning
                    additional concessions in Brazil desired by our Navy, I have the honor to
                    transmit herewith a copy of part of a memorandum<anchor n="26" xml:id="d567-f1"
                    /> prepared for me by Rear Admiral Beauregard giving a summary of the main
                    recommendations “made by the blimp board which were forwarded to Washington with
                    Admiral Ingram’s concurrence and recommendation for earliest possible
                    commencement of work.”</p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Jefferson Caffery</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d567-f1" n="26" xml:id="d567-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed; recommendations were to establish a blimp base at Maceio” and mast
                    facilities at seven other places, and to establish partial facilities at each
                    base for one ship in earliest possible time.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
